### AeroSaga Mission Control & Telemetry REST API
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@missionId =

### 1. Create a New Mission
# @name createMission
POST {{baseUrl}}/missions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "droneId": "DR-02",
  "source": "Warehouse-Alpha",
  "destination": "Hospital-North"
}

### 2. Get All Missions
GET {{baseUrl}}/missions
Accept: application/json

### 3. Start Mission
# Initiates Temporal workflow and transitions mission to ACTIVE
POST {{baseUrl}}/missions/{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}/start
Accept: application/json

### 4. Get Mission Details by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/missions/{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Get Mission Status & Recovery Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/missions/{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}/status
Accept: application/json

### 6. Get Dedicated Mission Progress & Recovery Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/missions/{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}/progress
Accept: application/json

### 7. Update Mission Status (Drone Entering Recovery Phase)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/missions/{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}/status?status=RETURNING_TO_BASE
Accept: application/json

### 8. Update Mission Progress & Recovery Step
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/missions/{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}/progress
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "progress": 95.0,
  "currentStep": "Final approach to base",
  "recoveryStatus": "RETURNING_TO_BASE"
}

### 9. Complete Mission & Recovery
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/missions/{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}/status?status=COMPLETED
Accept: application/json

### 10. Ingest Drone Telemetry
POST {{baseUrl}}/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "droneId": "DR-02",
  "missionId": "{{createMission.response.body.missionId}}",
  "latitude": 19.0760,
  "longitude": 72.8777,
  "altitude": 120.0,
  "batteryLevel": 85.5
}

### 11. Get Latest Drone Telemetry
GET {{baseUrl}}/telemetry/drone/DR-02/latest
Accept: application/json